{
  "_README": [
    "TEMPLATE, not a drop-in. Merge the parts you want into your own",
    "~/.claude/settings.json; do not copy this file over yours.",
    "",
    "Replace <PYTHON_EXE> with an absolute path to a Python 3.10+ interpreter and",
    "<CLAUDE_HOME> with the absolute path to your .claude directory. Claude Code",
    "does not expand ~ or environment variables inside a hook command, which is",
    "why these are absolute and why they are the only machine-bound values here.",
    "",
    "The permissions block is ONE operator's threat model, published as a worked",
    "example. Read every line before adopting it; an allowlist you did not decide",
    "on is worse than no allowlist. The `ask` entries are the important half —",
    "they make the config edit itself a confirmed action.",
    "",
    "env.CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW widens the auto-compact trigger to 400k",
    "tokens. The compact-recovery mechanism's bands (context_runway_shadow.py:",
    "150k/300k) and its own docstrings are calibrated assuming this window; drop",
    "the key (or lower it) and the notices simply fire earlier relative to the",
    "platform default, nothing breaks.",
    "",
    "OMISSIONS, named rather than left pointing at files you do not have (all",
    "declared in tools/share-manifest.toml with a reason):",
    "  · the three external-dispatch hooks (extdispatch_entrypoint_guard.py,",
    "    extdispatch_route_shadow.py, codex_dispatch_guard.py) — they gate a",
    "    dispatcher this share does not ship;",
    "  · session_board_register.py — one half of a source-environment tool (the",
    "    session board) that does not ship; the rule it serves degrades to the",
    "    by-hand steps stated in claude-ops/ops/20-dispatch.md §7a;",
    "  · user_profile_gist.py and registry_row_guard.py — the first injects a",
    "    personal profile of one operator, the second imports it as its parser",
    "    and refuses a registry row that has no row in that profile, so it is",
    "    inert (and its self-test fails) without it. project_registry_gist.py",
    "    ships alone and covers the registry digest;",
    "  · past_work_recall_inject.py and subagent_retrieval_brief.py — both read",
    "    the operator's personal memory silos through a recall tool that does",
    "    not ship;",
    "  · moc_closeout_notice.py and deliverable_birth_notice.py — each is bound",
    "    to a source-only index tree or graph snapshot;",
    "  · xi_card_guard.py — a shadow probe for a cross-index pipeline this",
    "    share does not carry; it is unmounted at the source too;",
    "  · the SessionEnd memory-pipeline mount — its script ships as",
    "    compact-recovery/preserve.py, but the mount still points outside",
    "    hooks/ and this template mounts hooks/ and nothing else; the optional",
    "    SessionEnd block lives in compact-recovery/README.md.",
    "",
    "Tool-backed hooks. Several mounted hooks call a method tool by its source",
    "path (tools/<name>/...): the tools ship under instruments/<name>/ in this",
    "repo, so copy each one to <CLAUDE_HOME>/tools/<name>/ before relying on the",
    "hook that cites it. Three of them also read a registry that ships as a",
    "template (system-hmi registry/subsystems.json, view-launcher views.json,",
    "references/PROJECTS.md); until you fill it they stay silent or say so.",
    "A hook whose tool is absent degrades to silence or a one-line notice; it",
    "never blocks. unattended_run.py is the exception worth knowing: its Stop",
    "guard blocks the end of a session ONLY while an [unattended-run] manifest",
    "is armed and no run report exists, and that state is created only by the",
    "kickoff hook beside it.",
    "",
    "Every hook in hooks/ that is MOUNTED AT THE SOURCE and ships is mounted",
    "here — if you find one that is not, that is a defect in this template, not",
    "a recommendation. Four .py files directly under hooks/ are deliberately NOT",
    "mounted, none is a defect: hooks/deny_receipt.py and hooks/handoff_snapshot.py",
    "are plain shared libraries (deny/notice receipt clauses; snapshot_path,",
    "is_fresh, notice) imported by other hooks — each has no event to mount at,",
    "the same way a Python module you import is not itself wired into an event;",
    "hooks/fieldwork_threshold_notice.py (retired 2026-09-11, user ruling R-3) and",
    "hooks/delivery_gate_shadow.py (retired at the source 2026-09-27, its",
    "SubagentStop mount removed) are retired probes — files and telemetry shapes",
    "are kept for provenance and rollback, but no mount exists to carry over, and",
    "this template mirrors that. The regression suites under hooks/tests/ are run",
    "by hand (`python hooks/tests/<name>.py`), not hooks — mounting a test as a",
    "hook would put a test harness on every matched tool call.",
    "",
    "Verify after wiring: run each hook by hand with empty stdin and check it",
    "exits 0 (they are all fail-open), then confirm the matcher fires on a real",
    "call. A hook registered at a path that does not exist makes python exit 2,",
    "which Claude Code treats as a blocking error for every matched tool call."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(git status:*)",
      "Bash(git log:*)",
      "Bash(git diff:*)",
      "Bash(git branch:*)",
      "Bash(git show:*)",
      "Bash(git add *)",
      "Bash(git commit *)",
      "Bash(mkdir *)",
      "Bash(npx vitest *)",
      "Bash(npx tsc *)",
      "Bash(npx oxlint *)",
      "Bash(npm test)",
      "mcp__Claude_Browser__read_page",
      "mcp__Claude_Browser__read_console_messages",
      "mcp__Claude_Browser__get_page_text",
      "mcp__Claude_Browser__find",
      "mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_logs",
      "WebSearch"
    ],
    "ask": [
      "Edit(~/.claude/CLAUDE.md)",
      "Edit(~/.claude/settings.json)",
      "Edit(~/.claude/settings.local.json)",
      "Edit(~/.claude/hooks/**)",
      "Edit(~/.claude/rules/**)"
    ]
  },
  "model": "haiku",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Read|Grep|Bash|PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/secret_file_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash|PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/dangerous_command_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/shell_transport_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/branch_commit_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5,
            "if": "Bash(*git*)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/appdata_view_guard.py\""
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/dispatch_commit_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5,
            "if": "Bash(*git*)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/branch_commit_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5,
            "if": "PowerShell(*git*)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/dispatch_commit_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5,
            "if": "PowerShell(*git*)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Agent|Workflow",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/model_cap_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/dispatch_commit_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/verbatim_dispatch_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__(Claude_Browser|claude-in-chrome)__(computer|javascript_tool)",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/ui_verify_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__(Claude_Browser|claude-in-chrome)__(navigate|preview_start)",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/browser_pane_scope_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "WebFetch|Bash|PowerShell|mcp__(Claude_Browser|claude-in-chrome)__(navigate|preview_start|browser_batch)|mcp__playwright-headless__browser_navigate",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/literature_host_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/ps_errorpref_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/ps_pipeline_close_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/unattended_run.py\" scope",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/boundary_contract_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/feedback_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Read",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/transcript_read_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|Bash|PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/intake_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/published_record_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|NotebookEdit|Bash|PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/worktree_scope_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 6
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__.*__search_session_transcripts",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/session_search_query_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__(Claude_Browser|claude-in-chrome)__javascript_tool",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/ui_verify_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/golive_check.py\"",
            "timeout": 150
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/compact_bookmark.py\"",
            "timeout": 60
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostCompact": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/compact_loss_record.py\"",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/ops_health_nudge.py\"",
            "timeout": 3
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/project_registry_gist.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/view_launcher_gist.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/worktree_scope_guard.py\"",
            "timeout": 8
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/system_hmi_summary.py\"",
            "timeout": 3
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/tree_noise_gist.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "compact",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/compact_pointer.py\"",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/dispatch_commit_notice.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "InstructionsLoaded": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/instructions_loaded_logger.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/context_runway_shadow.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/unattended_run.py\" kickoff",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/intake_match_shadow.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"<PYTHON_EXE>\" \"<CLAUDE_HOME>/hooks/unattended_run.py\" stop",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "disableWorkflows": true,
  "effortLevel": "medium",
  "switchModelsOnFlag": false,
  "cleanupPeriodDays": 3650,
  "env": {
    "CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB": "0",
    "CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW": "400000"
  }
}
